<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-386] Download pages does not say what to download</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-386</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The download page only points to the generic ASF download page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It&apos;s not at all clear what the user is supposed to download; there&apos;s just a list of file names.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;zeppelin-0.5.0-incubating-bin-spark-1.3.1_hadoop-2.3.tgz&lt;br/&gt;
zeppelin-0.5.0-incubating-bin-spark-1.4.0_hadoop-2.3.tgz&lt;br/&gt;
zeppelin-0.5.0-incubating.tgz                           &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Which of these am I supposed to download?&lt;br/&gt;
I&apos;m guessing that the last file is the source, because it is much smaller, but what are the other two? Do I need them both?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Most projects include a custom download page which provides direct links to the artifacts, for example see:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://camel.apache.org/download.html&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://camel.apache.org/download.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;http://httpd.apache.org/download.cgi&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://httpd.apache.org/download.cgi&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;http://tomcat.apache.org/download-80.cgi&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://tomcat.apache.org/download-80.cgi&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For more details on setting up a customised page, please see:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.apache.org/dev/release-download-pages.html#custom&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://www.apache.org/dev/release-download-pages.html#custom&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Note that download pages should link to the KEYS file and to hashes and sigs for each download. See the above example pages.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://zeppelin.incubator.apache.org/download.html&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://zeppelin.incubator.apache.org/download.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</environment>
